<xml>
  <block type="lcd_user_init" x="30" y="30">
    <field name="ADDR">0x27</field>
    <field name="COLS">20</field>
    <field name="ROWS">4</field>
    <next>
      <block type="lcd_user_print">
        <field name="COL">0</field>
        <field name="ROW">0</field>
        <value name="CONTENT">
          <block type="text">
            <field name="TEXT">A0 potentiometer</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <next>
          <block type="lcd_user_print">
            <field name="COL">0</field>
            <field name="ROW">1</field>
            <value name="CONTENT">
              <block type="text">
                <field name="TEXT">Value:</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="lcd_user_print">
                <field name="COL">9</field>
                <field name="ROW">1</field>
                <value name="CONTENT">
                  <block type="text">
                    <field name="TEXT">    </field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="lcd_user_print">
                    <field name="COL">9</field>
                    <field name="ROW">1</field>
                    <value name="CONTENT">
                      <block type="inout_analog_read">
                        <field name="PIN">A0</field>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Measure the voltage on this analog input. On ATmega168/328, the ADC returns 0–1023; other boards may use a different ADC range. A potentiometer wiper or analog sensor connects here.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <next>
                      <block type="base_delay">
                        <value name="DELAY_TIME">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">250</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Wait for the given number of milliseconds (1000 ms = 1 second). This pauses the main program; avoid long waits when loop must service motors, music files or serial input.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </next>
                  </block>
                </next>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </next>
    <comment pinned="false" w="480" h="240">Purpose: Show a potentiometer reading on a 20×4 LCD. Use the named LCD and buffer examples for reusable display logic.
Wiring: lcd user init: address 0x27; analog read: PIN A0; I2C SDA A4, SCL A5; Potentiometer outer legs VCC/GND; wiper on the listed analog input. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Turn A0 and change which LCD row shows the ADC reading.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
